# MCP image (node:22-slim) — Debian bookworm base + npm transitive CVEs.
# Revisit on each Node image bump. Tracked for quarterly review in the main
# repo's audits/MASTER-SECURITY-ISSUES-REVIEW.md under "Dockerfile base image
# CVE ignores (vault + mcp)".

# npm tar / tar-fs / transitive CVEs — pending fixed releases from upstream.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# glibc memalign — no bookworm security update; pulled transitively.
CVE-2026-0861

# zlib — Debian "will_not_fix" for minizip path; MCP binary does not use the
# affected minizip API.
CVE-2023-45853

# nghttp2 HTTP/2 DoS via malformed frames — unfixed in bookworm. Ingress path
# is not exposed: Cloud Run terminates HTTP/2 at the frontend. Outbound path
# only reaches api.1claw.xyz (our own Vault) over HTTP/1.1. Residual risk:
# low. Accepted until Debian patches or we migrate the MCP image base.
CVE-2026-27135

# systemd libsystemd0 / libudev1 ACE — unfixed in bookworm. Not reachable:
# container has no systemd init; libs linked only transitively.
CVE-2026-29111

# ncurses buffer overflow via terminal escape sequences — unfixed in bookworm.
# MCP runs headless with no TTY; ncurses linked transitively only.
CVE-2025-69720

# libcap2 privilege escalation via TOCTOU race in cap_set_file() — unfixed in
# bookworm (libcap2 1:2.66-4+deb12u2+b2). The vulnerable codepath sets file
# capabilities. MCP container runs only the Node fastmcp server; never invokes
# cap_set_file (no setcap, no privilege drops). Library is pulled transitively
# and never called. Accepted.
CVE-2026-4878

# libgcrypt20 DoS / buffer overflow via crafted ECDH ciphertext — unfixed in
# bookworm (libgcrypt20 1.10.1-3). MCP's outbound TLS goes through Node's
# OpenSSL; libgcrypt is not used. Pulled transitively (gnutls / libldap chain)
# and the affected ECDH function is never called. Accepted.
CVE-2026-41989

# gnutls DTLS zero-length fragment DoS — unfixed in bookworm (libgnutls30
# 3.7.9-2+deb12u6). MCP does not use DTLS or TLS via gnutls; all TLS goes
# through Node's bundled OpenSSL. libgnutls pulled transitively, unreachable.
# DoS-only, no RCE. Accepted.
CVE-2026-33845

# gnutls name constraint handling security bypass — unfixed in bookworm. MCP
# uses Node's OpenSSL for all TLS; gnutls is a transitive dep, never invoked.
CVE-2026-42010
CVE-2026-42011
# libgnutls30 HIGH CVEs — no fixed version in bookworm; gnutls never used by MCP.
CVE-2026-33846
CVE-2026-3833

# libssh2 integer overflow — unfixed in bookworm. MCP performs no SSH
# connections; libssh2 pulled transitively and never called. Accepted.
CVE-2026-7598

# curl / libcurl4 — unfixed in bookworm. MCP's HTTP client is Node's fetch
# (undici); system curl/libcurl is base-image only and never used for requests.
# CVE-2026-5773: SMB wrong-transfer — MCP never speaks SMB. CVE-2026-6276:
# libcurl cookie-leak — MCP does not use libcurl. Accepted.
CVE-2026-5773
CVE-2026-6276

# perl-base (Archive::Tar / IO-Compress) — fix_deferred/affected in bookworm.
# MCP is a headless Node server; perl and its modules are base-image only and
# never invoked at runtime. Vulnerable paths require parsing attacker-controlled
# archives in perl, which MCP never does. Accepted.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-9538
# CVE-2026-13221: Perl silently incorrect output (CRITICAL). Base-image only.
CVE-2026-13221
# CVE-2026-57433/57432: Storable/pack perl CVEs. Base-image only.
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-57432

# curl / libcurl4 — additional bookworm CVEs; MCP uses Node fetch, not libcurl.
CVE-2026-8458
CVE-2026-8927
CVE-2026-8286
CVE-2026-12064

# gzip LZH overflow — base image only; MCP never invokes gzip CLI.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 symlink traversal — base image only.
CVE-2026-54369

# util-linux / libblkid partition parser overflow — base image only.
CVE-2026-53615

# npm transitive CVEs — pending upstream lockfile resolution in fastmcp deps.
# brace-expansion DoS (HIGH) — deep transitive via glob/minimatch chain.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152
# fast-uri host confusion — overridden to 3.1.5+ but Trivy may still flag
# intermediate copies until lockfile refresh; accepted at MCP proxy boundary.
CVE-2026-13676
CVE-2026-16221
CVE-2026-18446
# ip-address parsing inconsistency — deep transitive.
CVE-2026-69192
